{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Example OAuth client registry for TrustedRisk multi-tenant deployment.",
    "Copy to oauth_clients.json and replace the example secrets before enabling OAuth.",
    "",
    "client_secret_hash format is `sha256:<hex>`. Generate one with:",
    "  python -c \"from mcp_server.oauth import OAuthClient; print(OAuthClient.hash_secret('YOUR-SECRET'))\"",
    "",
    "allowed_fhir_servers is the multi-tenant isolation guard: a client with",
    "tenant=tenant-a CANNOT use its bearer token to query tenant-b's FHIR endpoint",
    "(see test_oauth.py::test_middleware_blocks_cross_tenant_fhir).",
    "",
    "An empty allowed_fhir_servers list means *wildcard* — used for trusted",
    "internal clients only.",
    "",
    "Recognised scopes (clients SHOULD request only what they need):",
    "  discharge.read     — invoke compute_readmission_risk + utility",
    "  discharge.execute  — same plus medication_reconciliation + fairness_audit",
    "  phi.scan           — invoke detect_phi only",
    "  grounding.read     — invoke ground_claim only"
  ],
  "clients": [
    {
      "client_id": "tenant-a-orchestrator",
      "client_secret_hash": "sha256:REPLACE_ME_with_actual_hash",
      "tenant": "tenant-a",
      "allowed_scopes": ["discharge.read", "discharge.execute", "phi.scan", "grounding.read"],
      "allowed_fhir_servers": ["https://tenant-a.fhir.example.com/baseR4"]
    },
    {
      "client_id": "tenant-b-discharge-bot",
      "client_secret_hash": "sha256:REPLACE_ME_with_actual_hash",
      "tenant": "tenant-b",
      "allowed_scopes": ["discharge.read", "phi.scan"],
      "allowed_fhir_servers": ["https://tenant-b.fhir.example.com/baseR4"]
    },
    {
      "client_id": "internal-trustedrisk-self-test",
      "client_secret_hash": "sha256:REPLACE_ME_with_actual_hash",
      "tenant": "internal",
      "allowed_scopes": ["discharge.read", "discharge.execute", "phi.scan", "grounding.read"],
      "allowed_fhir_servers": []
    }
  ]
}
